**Fix formatPrice(cents)**

This doesn't compile: the return type says `string` but the body returns a number. Return the price as dollars with two decimals, e.g. 1250 → `"$12.50"`.

```ts
function formatPrice(cents: number): string {
  return cents / 100;
}
```

back:
// Why: A return type annotation turns "returns the wrong kind of value" into a compile
// error at the function, instead of a bug wherever it is used. toFixed(2) keeps "12.50".
// Docs: https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/2/everyday-types.html
function formatPrice(cents: number): string {
  return `$${(cents / 100).toFixed(2)}`;
}

starter_code:
